WEBVTT

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:05.595
Vision models keep asking one question: how
much of this patch looks like an edge?

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:09.648
To answer it, treat each image as an arrow, a
list of numbers.

00:00:09.668 --> 00:00:13.580
A patch has dozens of numbers, so let's shrink
it down to two.

00:00:14.155 --> 00:00:16.210
Here's x: three right, four up.

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:19.310
And here's a direction we care about, the
green line.

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:22.330
Which point on that line is closest to the tip
of x?

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:23.198
Let's search.

00:00:23.218 --> 00:00:26.460
Slide a point along the line, and watch the
dashed distance.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:29.555
It falls, bottoms out, then rises again.

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:33.908
At the best spot, the dashed line meets the
green line at a right angle.

00:00:33.928 --> 00:00:35.857
Anywhere else, it leans.

00:00:35.878 --> 00:00:38.965
So the closest point is where you drop a
perpendicular.

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:41.915
Picture light shining straight down onto the
line.

00:00:41.935 --> 00:00:46.560
The arrow casts a shadow, and that orange
shadow is the projection, p.

00:00:46.585 --> 00:00:50.178
To measure it, take a unit arrow, u, along the
line.

00:00:50.198 --> 00:00:53.315
The dot product of x with u is six over root
five,

00:00:53.335 --> 00:00:57.202
plus four over root five, about four point
four seven.

00:00:57.223 --> 00:01:01.085
Walk that far along u, and you land at the
point four, two.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:02.200
Quick check.

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:05.762
Suppose the line ran flat, along the
horizontal axis.

00:01:05.782 --> 00:01:07.162
Where would the shadow end?

00:01:07.182 --> 00:01:08.820
Pause and decide.

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:12.962
It ends at three.

00:01:12.982 --> 00:01:15.950
A flat line keeps only the first coordinate.

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:18.675
Now turn the line, and the shadow follows.

00:01:18.695 --> 00:01:23.220
Its tip even traces a circle, because the
corner is always a right angle.

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:26.888
The part the shadow misses is the residual, r.

00:01:26.908 --> 00:01:31.138
It is perpendicular to the line, so r dot u is
zero.

00:01:31.158 --> 00:01:34.320
Shadow plus residual rebuilds x exactly.

00:01:34.745 --> 00:01:36.025
Back to images.

00:01:36.045 --> 00:01:41.563
With the patch as x and an edge template as u,
the dot product is the edge response.

00:01:41.583 --> 00:01:44.900
A convolution filter computes it at every
position.

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:49.620
And least squares asks the same question, with
a plane instead of a line.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:52.343
So remember three things.

00:01:52.363 --> 00:01:55.668
A dot product with a unit vector measures a
shadow.

00:01:55.688 --> 00:01:58.005
The shadow's tip is the closest point.

00:01:58.025 --> 00:02:00.375
And the leftover is perpendicular.

